# Keep the build context to the Go sources the root Dockerfile actually needs.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the context is the whole
# working tree — measured at over 1GB and still climbing on a developer machine
# (web-v2/node_modules alone is ~465MB, .git ~249MB), none of which the Go build
# reads. That cost was invisible while deploy/compose only ever PULLED a
# published image; it became the first thing a self-hoster waits on once that
# service learned to build locally.
#
# Anything the build genuinely needs must NOT be listed here: go.mod, go.sum,
# cmd/, internal/, and any embedded assets.

# VCS
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Frontend — the dashboard is a separate image (deploy/compose/Dockerfile.dashboard)
# and nothing in the Go build reads it.
web-v2/node_modules
web-v2/dist
web-v2/.vite
node_modules

# Local tooling / agent scratch
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Build outputs and local binaries (the repo tracks a prebuilt velox-bootstrap;
# the image builds its own from source)
velox-bootstrap
bin/
dist/
*.test
*.out
coverage*

# Docs, screenshots and walk artifacts — large and irrelevant to the binary
*.md
docs/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf

# Local env / secrets must never enter an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS noise
.DS_Store
